---
import "../styles/global.css";

const canonicalURL = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site);
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="What is a schema? Why do schemas matter? How are schemas defined? Engrams is the cognitive schema engine that gives AI agents architectural mental models before they write code."
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href={canonicalURL} />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>Engrams — Cognitive Schemas for AI Agents</title>
  </head>
  <body class="signal-body">
    <!-- ── TOP BAR ── -->
    <header class="top-bar">
      <div class="bar-inner">
        <a href="/" class="brand">
          <span class="glyph">⬡</span>
          <span class="name">ENGRAMS</span>
          <span class="version">v0.14.0</span>
        </a>
        <nav class="nav">
          <a href="#what">What is a Schema</a>
          <a href="#why">Why Schemas Matter</a>
          <a href="#how">How Schemas are Defined</a>
          <a href="/docs/guide/cognitive-schemas" class="highlight">Guide</a>
          <a href="/docs/getting-started">Docs</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/stevebrownlee/engrams-cli" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub ↗</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="page-content">
      <!-- ══ 1. THE HERO MANIFESTO ══ -->
      <section class="hero-signal">
        <div class="signal-kicker">COGNITIVE SCHEMA ENGINE // ARCHITECTURAL RUNTIME FOR AI AGENTS</div>
        <h1 class="signal-title">
          AI models don't fail because they can't code.<br />
          <span class="accent">They fail because they lack mental models.</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="signal-lede">
          Engrams is the schema runtime for your codebase. It formalizes your architectural intent into
          <strong>Cognitive Schemas</strong> — compact, high-level mental models that tell your AI agent
          how your system works before it writes a single line of code.
        </p>

        <div class="signal-actions">
          <a href="/docs/quick-start" class="btn-action primary">Quick Start in 5 Minutes</a>
          <a href="/docs/guide/cognitive-schemas" class="btn-action ghost">Read the Full Guide</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ══ 2. WHAT IS A SCHEMA? ══ -->
      <section id="what" class="content-section">
        <div class="section-label">PART 01 // THE DEFINITION</div>
        <h2 class="section-heading">What is a Schema?</h2>
        <p class="section-description">
          A Cognitive Schema is an <strong>active mental model</strong>, not a passive document.
          Just as a human engineer carries intuition about how code should behave, a schema formalizes
          three exact elements into a single machine-retrievable concept:
        </p>

        <div class="specimen-card">
          <div class="sc-header">
            <div class="sc-title">
              <span class="sc-badge">SCHEMA</span>
              <code>payment-adapters</code>
            </div>
            <span class="sc-status">● active concept · local SQLite</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sc-content">
            <div class="sc-row">
              <span class="sc-k">⚡ TRIGGER</span>
              <div class="sc-v">
                <strong>When does this concept apply?</strong>
                <p>Fires when editing payment adapter implementations under <code>src/adapters/</code></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="sc-row">
              <span class="sc-k">📋 DIRECTIVE</span>
              <div class="sc-v">
                <strong>What invariant must be followed?</strong>
                <p class="rule-box">
                  Implement PaymentProvider trait; pass idempotency_key to all charge requests; verify signatures with crypto::constant_time_eq; never log raw payload tokens.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="sc-row">
              <span class="sc-k">🔗 MEMBERS</span>
              <div class="sc-v">
                <strong>What decisions and code anchors prove why?</strong>
                <div class="sc-members">
                  <span class="m-pill">ADR #44: PaymentProvider interface contract</span>
                  <span class="m-pill">Pattern #8: Constant-time signature verification</span>
                  <span class="m-pill anchor">Anchor: src/adapters/stripe.rs</span>
                  <span class="m-pill anchor">Anchor: src/billing/service.rs</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="anatomy-grid">
          <div class="anatomy-item">
            <h3>1. The Activation Trigger</h3>
            <p>
              A testable condition an agent can evaluate from context alone (e.g., target file paths or task tags).
              Schemas don't float in global context; they wake up precisely when relevant.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="anatomy-item">
            <h3>2. The Operational Directive</h3>
            <p>
              An imperative instruction the AI executes immediately. Not passive history, but a concrete operational
              rule that prevents bugs, security leaks, and convention drift.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="anatomy-item">
            <h3>3. Bundled Knowledge Members</h3>
            <p>
              The underlying decisions, patterns, and code anchors that ground the rule. If the AI needs to know <em>why</em>
              the rule exists, the contracts and reasoning are already linked.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ══ 3. WHY SCHEMAS MATTER ══ -->
      <section id="why" class="content-section">
        <div class="section-label">PART 02 // THE COGNITIVE THESIS</div>
        <h2 class="section-heading">Why Schemas Matter</h2>
        <p class="section-description">
          Senior engineers don't re-read the entire company manual before writing a function.
          They rely on mental models built from months of experience. Today's AI tools treat your agent
          like a perpetual novice. Schemas change the fundamental dynamics of agentic coding:
        </p>

        <div class="pillar-grid">
          <div class="pillar-card">
            <span class="pillar-num">01</span>
            <h3>From Syntax Scraping to Conceptual Clarity</h3>
            <p>
              Without schemas, an AI agent opens 10 to 15 source files defensively, burning thousands of tokens
              just trying to reverse-engineer your conventions from raw syntax. With schemas, the AI receives
              the exact mental model in <strong>under 300 tokens on Turn 1</strong> before touching code.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="pillar-card">
            <span class="pillar-num">02</span>
            <h3>Invariants Enforced Before Code is Written</h3>
            <p>
              Don't catch architectural violations during human pull request review. When an agent touches a file,
              <code>engrams advise</code> intercepts the edit and provides the non-negotiable architectural directives upfront.
              The agent writes compliant code on the first attempt.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="pillar-card">
            <span class="pillar-num">03</span>
            <h3>Compounding Codebase Intuition</h3>
            <p>
              Chat transcripts vanish. Documentation goes stale. Cognitive Schemas live in local SQLite and
              compound with every session. As your graph densifies, Engrams shifts from passively answering queries
              to actively steering your agent with the accumulated intuition of your team.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ══ 4. HOW SCHEMAS ARE DEFINED ══ -->
      <section id="how" class="content-section">
        <div class="section-label">PART 03 // THE LIFECYCLE</div>
        <h2 class="section-heading">How Schemas are Defined</h2>
        <p class="section-description">
          Schemas do not require tedious manual database administration. Engrams detects them from normal git work,
          nudges you at session close, and enforces a strict trigger-and-rule contract.
        </p>

        <div class="how-steps">
          <!-- Step 1 -->
          <div class="how-step">
            <div class="hs-marker">
              <span class="hs-num">1</span>
            </div>
            <div class="hs-content">
              <h3>Autonomous Graph Detection</h3>
              <p>
                As you commit code and record architectural decisions, Engrams runs graph community detection
                to identify natural clusters of co-edited files and related rules:
              </p>
              <pre class="hs-code"><code># Detect clusters from your codebase graph and stage candidates
$ engrams schema scan</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 2 -->
          <div class="how-step">
            <div class="hs-marker">
              <span class="hs-num">2</span>
            </div>
            <div class="hs-content">
              <h3>Session-End Opportunity Nudges</h3>
              <p>
                You don't need to remember to check for schemas. When you run <code>session close</code>, Engrams
                spots qualified candidates and prints a ready-to-run confirm command with a suggested kebab-case name:
              </p>
              <pre class="hs-code"><code>$ engrams session close --pr 42
&#123;
  "schema_opportunities": [
    &#123;
      "suggested_name": "payment-adapters",
      "confirm_command": "engrams schema confirm decision:10,dec --name payment-adapters"
    &#125;
  ]
&#125;</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 3 -->
          <div class="how-step">
            <div class="hs-marker">
              <span class="hs-num">3</span>
            </div>
            <div class="hs-content">
              <h3>Standardized Refinement: Trigger + Rule</h3>
              <p>
                A schema summary is an activation contract. Refinement requires an explicit trigger condition
                and an operational directive, immediately ranking it above machine drafts:
              </p>
              <pre class="hs-code"><code>$ engrams schema refine payment-adapters \
  --trigger "editing payment adapter implementations" \
  --rule "implement PaymentProvider; use crypto::constant_time_eq"</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Step 4 -->
          <div class="how-step">
            <div class="hs-marker">
              <span class="hs-num">4</span>
            </div>
            <div class="hs-content">
              <h3>Pre-Edit Interception</h3>
              <p>
                Tomorrow, your AI touches <code>src/adapters/stripe.rs</code>. Coding harnesses (omp, Cursor, Claude Code)
                run <code>engrams advise</code>. The schema fires automatically in 1ms:
              </p>
              <pre class="hs-code"><code>$ engrams advise src/adapters/stripe.rs
&#123;
  "schemas": [
    &#123;
      "name": "payment-adapters",
      "summary": "Fires when editing payment adapters: implement PaymentProvider..."
    &#125;
  ],
  "constraints": [ ... ]
&#125;</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ══ 5. INSTALL & ACTION ══ -->
      <section class="install-section">
        <div class="install-box">
          <h2>Give your AI the mental models it deserves.</h2>
          <p>Local SQLite engine. 0MB background memory. 1ms query execution.</p>
          <div class="install-code">
            <code>cargo install engrams-cli</code>
            <span class="sep">or</span>
            <code>brew install stevebrownlee/tap/engrams</code>
          </div>
          <div class="install-actions">
            <a href="/docs/quick-start" class="btn-action primary">5-Minute Quick Start</a>
            <a href="/docs/guide/cognitive-schemas" class="btn-action ghost">Read the Schema Guide</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <!-- ── MINIMAL FOOTER ── -->
    <footer class="bottom-footer">
      <div class="footer-wrap">
        <span>⬡ ENGRAMS · Apache-2.0 · Cognitive Schema Engine for AI Agents</span>
        <div class="footer-links">
          <a href="/docs/guide/cognitive-schemas">Cognitive Schemas</a>
          <a href="/docs/getting-started">Docs</a>
          <a href="/docs/reference/cli">CLI Reference</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/stevebrownlee/engrams-cli" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  /* ============================================================
     MAXIMUM SIGNAL: SCHEMAS-FIRST ARCHITECTURAL LEDGER
     Focus: 1. What is a schema? 2. Why schemas matter? 3. How schemas are defined?
     ============================================================ */

  :root {
    --bg-dark: #080a0f;
    --bg-surface: #0e121a;
    --bg-elevated: #131824;
    --border-dim: #1e2636;
    --border-bright: #2d384e;
    --text-white: #ffffff;
    --text-body: #e2e8f0;
    --text-muted: #8e9bb0;
    --brass: #cca43b;
    --brass-bright: #f3ba42;
    --green: #4ade80;
    --font-mono: 'SFMono-Regular', Consolas, 'Liberation Mono', Menlo, monospace;
    --font-sans: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
  }

  .signal-body {
    background: var(--bg-dark);
    color: var(--text-body);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }

  /* ── TOP BAR ── */
  .top-bar {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0; left: 0; right: 0;
    z-index: 100;
    background: rgba(8, 10, 15, 0.96);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-dim);
    backdrop-filter: blur(8px);
  }
  .bar-inner {
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .brand { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.4rem; text-decoration: none; color: var(--text-white); }
  .glyph { color: var(--brass-bright); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .name { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 900; font-size: 1rem; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
  .version { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-left: 0.2rem; }
  .nav { display: flex; gap: 1.4rem; }
  .nav a { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--text-muted); text-decoration: none; transition: color 0.15s; }
  .nav a:hover { color: var(--text-white); }
  .nav a.highlight { color: var(--brass-bright); font-weight: 700; }
  @media (max-width: 700px) { .nav a:not(:last-child):not(.highlight) { display: none; } }

  /* ── MAIN CONTENT CONTAINER ── */
  .page-content {
    max-width: 68rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 7.5rem 1.5rem 4rem;
  }

  /* ── 1. HERO ── */
  .hero-signal {
    margin-bottom: 5.5rem;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .signal-kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    color: var(--brass-bright);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
  }
  .signal-title {
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 5.5vw, 4.2rem);
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: var(--text-white);
    margin: 0 0 1.6rem;
  }
  .signal-title .accent { color: var(--brass-bright); }
  .signal-lede {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--text-body);
    max-width: 50rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.2rem;
  }
  .signal-lede strong { color: var(--text-white); }
  .signal-actions { display: flex; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }

  /* ── TECHNICAL BUTTONS (ZERO PILLS) ── */
  .btn-action {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 2px;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: all 0.15s;
  }
  .btn-action.primary {
    background: var(--brass-bright);
    color: #080a0f;
    border-color: var(--brass-bright);
  }
  .btn-action.primary:hover {
    background: #ffcf54;
    box-shadow: 0 0 16px rgba(243, 186, 66, 0.4);
  }
  .btn-action.ghost {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--text-body);
    border-color: var(--border-bright);
  }
  .btn-action.ghost:hover {
    border-color: var(--brass-bright);
    color: var(--brass-bright);
  }

  /* ── COMMON SECTION HEADERS ── */
  .content-section {
    margin-bottom: 6rem;
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-dim);
  }
  .section-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    color: var(--brass-bright);
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
  }
  .section-heading {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--text-white);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .section-description {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.65;
    max-width: 52rem;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  .section-description strong { color: var(--text-white); }

  /* ── 2. WHAT IS A SCHEMA (SPECIMEN CARD) ── */
  .specimen-card {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-dim);
    border-radius: 2px;
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
    box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
  }
  .sc-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.4rem;
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-dim);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }
  .sc-title { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.6rem; }
  .sc-badge {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    background: var(--brass-bright);
    color: #080a0f;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .sc-title code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text-white);
  }
  .sc-status {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    color: var(--green);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .sc-content { padding: 1.8rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.4rem; }
  .sc-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: baseline; }
  @media (max-width: 680px) { .sc-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.4rem; } }
  .sc-k {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--brass-bright);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .sc-v strong { display: block; font-size: 0.88rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-bottom: 0.25rem; font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .sc-v p { margin: 0; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--text-white); }
  .sc-v code { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--brass-bright); font-size: 0.9em; }
  .rule-box {
    font-family: var(--font-mono) !important;
    font-size: 0.92rem !important;
    background: rgba(204, 164, 59, 0.08);
    border: 1px solid rgba(204, 164, 59, 0.25);
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
    color: var(--text-white) !important;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .sc-members { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 0.4rem; }
  .m-pill {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    padding: 0.3rem 0.65rem;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-dim);
    color: var(--text-body);
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .m-pill.anchor { color: var(--green); border-color: rgba(74, 222, 128, 0.35); }

  .anatomy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .anatomy-item {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-dim);
    padding: 1.6rem;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }
  .anatomy-item h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-white); margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .anatomy-item p { font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; }
  .anatomy-item em { color: var(--text-white); font-style: normal; font-weight: 600; }

  /* ── 3. WHY SCHEMAS MATTER (PILLARS) ── */
  .pillar-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .pillar-card {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-dim);
    border-radius: 2px;
    padding: 2rem 1.8rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }
  .pillar-num {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--brass-bright);
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }
  .pillar-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--text-white);
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .pillar-card p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.65;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .pillar-card strong { color: var(--text-white); }
  .pillar-card code { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--brass-bright); }

  /* ── 4. HOW SCHEMAS ARE DEFINED (STEPS) ── */
  .how-steps {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.8rem;
  }
  .how-step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 48px 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-dim);
    border-radius: 2px;
    padding: 1.8rem;
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) { .how-step { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.75rem; } }
  .hs-marker {
    width: 38px; height: 38px;
    background: rgba(204, 164, 59, 0.12);
    border: 1px solid rgba(204, 164, 59, 0.35);
    border-radius: 2px;
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
    color: var(--brass-bright);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 900;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .hs-content h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-white); margin: 0 0 0.5rem; }
  .hs-content p { font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .hs-content code { font-family: var(--font-mono); color: var(--brass-bright); font-size: 0.88em; }
  .hs-code {
    background: #090c12;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-dim);
    border-radius: 2px;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.1rem;
    margin: 0;
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .hs-code code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-body);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

